        "tex": "-1 + \\sqrt{3}\\,i &= 2\\left(\\cos\\left(\\frac{2\\pi}{3} + 2n\\pi\\right) + i\\sin\\left(\\frac{2\\pi}{3} + 2n\\pi\\right)\\right)"
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "title": "Take the square root using De Moivre",
      "lines": [
       {
        "text": "$w = (-1 + \\sqrt{3}\\,i)^{1/2}$: raise the modulus to the power $\\tfrac12$ and multiply the angle by $\\tfrac12$."
       },
       {
        "tex": "w &= 2^{\\frac12}\\left(\\cos\\left(\\frac12\\left(\\frac{2\\pi}{3} + 2n\\pi\\right)\\right) + i\\sin\\left(\\frac12\\left(\\frac{2\\pi}{3} + 2n\\pi\\right)\\right)\\right)"
       },
       {
        "tex": "&= \\sqrt{2}\\left(\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3} + n\\pi\\right) + i\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3} + n\\pi\\right)\\right)"
